# INT-SOURCE: ../functional/65_neg_global.my
# INT-ENGINES: tw default nj noopt
#
# INT unit (#107) over tests/functional/65_neg_global.my:
# Unary minus on a GLOBAL, inside a function. A proven-int/float `-x` is a
# typed negation, and the typed path has no leaf for a global (a capture and
# a call result have one), so it falls back to the boxed tier - which knew
# `!x` but not `-x`.
#
# It runs as a coverage unit under the engines above, with no second
# copy (INT-SOURCE): code no other unit reaches. It asserts its own
# results, and every engine must print the same.
